ic Strecker to 2-amino-3-hydroxypropanenitrile, hydrolysis to serine", "description": "From glycolic acid (UV or Cannizzaro formaldehyde), conversion to aminonitrile intermediate, then surface hydrolysis to serine.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_013", "rxn_009", "rxn_010"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_012", "mol_014"]}, {"pathway_id": "P3", "name": "Hydrothermal glyoxylate reductive amination", "description": "Glyoxylate is reductively aminated by hydroxylamine and iron, yielding glycine; glycine then condenses with formaldehyde at hydrothermal vents to form serine.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_011", "rxn_007", "rxn_004"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_010", "mol_008"]}, {"pathway_id": "P4", "name": "Surface photochemical glyoxylate then reductive amination route", "description": "2,2-dihydroxyacetic acid is dehydrated by UV to yield glyoxylate, which undergoes iron-catalyzed reductive amination to give glycine, then to serine.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_012", "rxn_007", "rxn_004"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_010", "mol_008"]}, {"pathway_id": "P5", "name": "Surface N-methylene glycine Schiff base pathway", "description": "Glycine plus formaldehyde form N-methylene glycine, which upon formaldehyde addition and hydrolytic reduction yields serine.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_005", "rxn_006"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_007"]}, {"pathway_id": "P6", "name": "Hydrothermal peracetic acid route", "description": "Peracetic acid and ammonia combine to form glycine, which enters the main hydrothermal glycine-formaldehyde condensation to serine.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_015", "rxn_004"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_008"]}, {"pathway_id": "P7", "name": "Surface acetate photoredox to glycolic acid, Strecker aminonitrile route", "description": "UV photochemistry converts acetate into glycolic acid, which forms the aminonitrile intermediate, feeding into hydrolytic production of serine.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_014", "rxn_009", "rxn_010"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_012", "mol_